---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About AfghanTours"
  description="Licensed Afghan-American tour operator providing cultural, historical, photography, expedition, and business travel across Afghanistan."
>

  <PageHero
    eyebrow="AfghanTours Leadership"
    title="About AfghanTours"
    text="Real access built through years of ground operations, local partnerships, and a commitment to showing Afghanistan beyond the headlines."
    image="/assets/images/heroes/about/hero.webp"
    primaryHref="/tours"
    primaryLabel="Explore Tours"
    secondaryHref="/contact"
    secondaryLabel="Contact Us"
    height="min-h-[70vh]"
  />

  <!-- OUR STORY -->

  <section class="bg-[#fbf8f2] py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">

      <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-amber-700">
        Our Story
      </p>

      <h2 class="editorial-title mt-4 text-5xl md:text-7xl">
        Afghanistan Through Local Eyes
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-lg leading-9 text-stone-700">

        <p>
          AfghanTours is a licensed Afghan-American tourism company offering
          safe, meaningful, and culturally rich journeys across Afghanistan.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6">
          Founded by James “Amir” Sidiqi and Mohammad “Edrees” Rahimi,
          our team combines international experience with deep local knowledge
          to help visitors explore Afghanistan responsibly and confidently.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6">
          Since 2016, our founders have worked with international visitors,
          diplomatic missions, NGOs, journalists, researchers, business
          delegations, and travelers seeking authentic access to Afghanistan.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6">
          We believe tourism has the power to restore Afghanistan’s image,
          support local families, preserve cultural heritage, and create new
          opportunities for future generations.
        </p>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FOUNDERS -->

  <section class="bg-white py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6">

      <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-amber-700">
        Leadership
      </p>

      <h2 class="editorial-title mt-4 text-5xl">
        Meet The Founders
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">

        <!-- JAMES -->

        <article class="overflow-hidden rounded-[2rem] border border-stone-200 bg-white shadow-sm">

          <img
            src="/assets/images/people/guides/partner-james.webp"
            alt="James Amir Sidiqi"
            class="h-[320px] w-full object-cover object-center"
          />

          <div class="p-8">

            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-amber-700">
              Co-Founder
            </p>

            <h3 class="editorial-title mt-3 text-4xl">
              James “Amir” Sidiqi
            </h3>

            <p class="mt-5 leading-8 text-stone-700">
              Western-led operations experience in Afghanistan since 2010.
              His background spans logistics, mining, contracting, tourism,
              and expedition support throughout the country.
            </p>

            <p class="mt-5 leading-8 text-stone-700">
              Having coordinated complex operations across Afghanistan for
              more than a decade, he helps visitors navigate the country safely
              while experiencing Afghanistan beyond the headlines.
            </p>

            <p class="mt-5 leading-8 text-stone-700">
              His experience working with international organizations,
              diplomatic communities, tourism groups, and private sector
              partners provides AfghanTours with a unique combination of local
              access and international standards.
            </p>

          </div>

        </article>

        <!-- EDREES -->

        <article class="overflow-hidden rounded-[2rem] border border-stone-200 bg-white shadow-sm">

          <img
            src="/assets/images/people/guides/partner-edrees.webp"
            alt="Mohammad Edrees Rahimi"
            class="h-[320px] w-full object-cover object-[50%_15%]"
          />

          <div class="p-8">

            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-amber-700">
              Co-Founder
            </p>

            <h3 class="editorial-title mt-3 text-4xl">
              Mohammad “Edrees” Rahimi
            </h3>

            <p class="mt-5 leading-8 text-stone-700">
              Edrees provides local leadership, operational coordination,
              and cultural expertise throughout Afghanistan.
            </p>

            <p class="mt-5 leading-8 text-stone-700">
              His understanding of Afghan communities, traditions,
              provincial travel, and regional logistics helps ensure that
              every journey operates smoothly while remaining authentic.
            </p>

            <p class="mt-5 leading-8 text-stone-700">
              He serves as a bridge between travelers and local communities,
              helping visitors engage respectfully with Afghanistan's people,
              culture, and history.
            </p>

          </div>

        </article>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHY WE STARTED -->

  <section class="bg-[#fbf8f2] py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">

      <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-amber-700">
        Why We Started AfghanTours
      </p>

      <h2 class="editorial-title mt-4 text-5xl md:text-7xl">
        Showing Another Side of Afghanistan
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-lg leading-9 text-stone-700">

        <p>
          Afghanistan is often viewed through the lens of conflict.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6">
          We created AfghanTours to show another side of the country—its
          history, hospitality, landscapes, cultures, traditions, and people.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6">
          Our goal is not simply to move visitors from one destination to
          another. We aim to create meaningful experiences that foster
          understanding, respect, and genuine cultural exchange.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6">
          Every tour supports local drivers, guides, hotels, restaurants,
          artisans, and communities across Afghanistan.
        </p>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- MISSION VISION VALUES -->

  <section class="bg-white py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6">

      <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-amber-700">
        What Drives Us
      </p>

      <h2 class="editorial-title mt-4 text-5xl">
        Mission, Vision & Values
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3">

        <div class="rounded-[2rem] border border-stone-200 bg-[#fbf8f2] p-8">

          <h3 class="text-3xl font-black">
            Mission
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-5 leading-8 text-stone-700">
            To provide safe, authentic, respectful, and unforgettable
            journeys while ensuring tourism directly benefits Afghan
            communities.
          </p>

        </div>

        <div class="rounded-[2rem] border border-stone-200 bg-[#fbf8f2] p-8">

          <h3 class="text-3xl font-black">
            Vision
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-5 leading-8 text-stone-700">
            A thriving tourism sector where Afghanistan is rediscovered
            by travelers, historians, photographers, filmmakers,
            researchers, mountaineers, and diaspora families.
          </p>

        </div>

        <div class="rounded-[2rem] border border-stone-200 bg-[#fbf8f2] p-8">

          <h3 class="text-3xl font-black">
            Values
          </h3>

          <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-stone-700">
            <li>Integrity</li>
            <li>Hospitality</li>
            <li>Safety</li>
            <li>Respect</li>
            <li>Cultural Preservation</li>
            <li>Community Support</li>
          </ul>

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TRUST -->

  <section class="bg-[#06150f] py-24 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6">

      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[320px_1fr]">

        <div>
          <img
            src="/assets/images/logo/jtt-license.webp"
            alt="AfghanTours License"
            class="rounded-3xl"
          />
        </div>

        <div>

          <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-amber-500">
            Trust & Ground Operations
          </p>

          <h2 class="editorial-title mt-4 text-5xl text-white">
            Real Access Built on Experience
          </h2>

          <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">

            <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/10 p-6">
              Licensed Afghan Tour Operator
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/10 p-6">
              License No. ATO-KBL-1617
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/10 p-6">
              Kabul-Based Operations
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/10 p-6">
              AfghanTours Leadership
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/10 p-6">
              15+ Years of Ground Operations
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/10 p-6">
              Tourism • Logistics • Media • Expeditions
            </div>

          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- IMPACT -->

  <section class="bg-[#0d1d16] py-24 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 text-center">

      <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-amber-500">
        Impact Through Tourism
      </p>

      <h2 class="editorial-title mt-4 text-5xl text-white">
        Tourism Can Create Opportunity
      </h2>

      <p class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-9 text-stone-300">
        We believe visitors should leave Afghanistan having contributed
        something positive to the communities that welcomed them.
        Tourism supports local drivers, guides, hotels, restaurants,
        artisans, family-owned businesses, and communities throughout
        Afghanistan.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>